    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d169">

                <pb facs="0186" n="174" sameAs="frus:frus1943v05/pg174"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">821.24/440: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in
                        Colombia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-03-29">March 29, 1943</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>399. Your 516 of March 22.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d169-f1"/> The Board of Economic
                    Warfare is now certifying, and will continue during the 60-day period to certify
                    for shipment, only those materials listed in despatch no. 1582<anchor n="11"
                        xml:id="d169-f2"/> as importable. The Embassy should, however, bear in mind
                    that materials <pb facs="0187" n="175" xml:id="pg175"/> covered by general
                    license and weighing less than 2240 pounds do not require certification by the
                    Board of Economic Warfare and some such shipments, even though considered
                    non-essential, will undoubtedly continue to arrive until the Decentralization
                    Plan is fully effective.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d169-f1" n="10" xml:id="d169-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d169-f2" n="11" xml:id="d169-f2-content">
                <p>Not printed; this list was a selection of articles according to Schedule B.
                    Schedule B was a statistical classification of domestic and foreign commodities
                    exported from the United States, drawn up by the Bureau of the Census,
                    Department of Commerce.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
